NAME
    pwd - print the current working directory

SYNOPSIS
    pwd

DESCRIPTION
    Calls SYS_GETCWD and writes the result to stdout.

    There is also a shell builtin `pwd` that does the same thing
    without forking — the binary exists so that pipelines like
    `pwd | tr / -` work (because the binary is what gets forked
    and exec'd into the pipeline stage, not the builtin).

EXAMPLES
    pwd
    pwd | tr / -

EXIT STATUS
    0   cwd printed
    1   SYS_GETCWD failed

SEE ALSO
    sh(1), cd
